@startuml
title EventHub - Local container architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true

actor Participant
actor Organizer
actor "Global administrator" as GlobalAdmin
actor "Demo presenter\n(synthetic personas)" as DemoPresenter

rectangle "EventHub local Docker Compose runtime" {
  component "Identity & Access\nmock" as Identity <<mock>>
  component "Event Management\nJava 21 / Spring Boot" as Events <<executable>>
  component "Registration\nJava 21 / Spring Boot" as Registration <<executable>>
  component "Billing\nmock" as Billing <<mock>>
  component "Notification\nmock" as Notification <<mock>>
  component "Attendance & Certification\nPython / FastAPI" as Attendance <<executable>>
  component "Reporting\nPython / FastAPI" as Reporting <<executable>>
  component "Demo Web\nPython 3.12 / FastAPI\noptional presentation adapter" as DemoWeb <<presentation>>

  queue "RabbitMQ" as RabbitMQ

  node "PostgreSQL cluster\nseparate service credentials" as PostgreSQL {
    database "Event Management\nlogical database/schema" as EventData
    database "Registration\nlogical database/schema" as RegistrationData
    database "Attendance & Certification\nlogical database/schema" as AttendanceData
    database "Reporting projection\nlogical database/schema" as ReportingData
  }
}

Participant --> Events : public catalog
Participant --> Registration : own registration commands/queries
Participant --> Attendance : eligible check-in / certificate
Organizer --> Events : manage own events and activities
Organizer --> Reporting : own-organization reports
GlobalAdmin --> Events : cross-organization event operations
GlobalAdmin --> Reporting : cross-organization reports
DemoPresenter --> DemoWeb : server-rendered browser UI

DemoWeb --> Events : HTTP API\ncatalog / preparation
DemoWeb --> Registration : HTTP API\nregistration commands / queries
DemoWeb --> Attendance : HTTP API\ncheck-in / certificates
DemoWeb --> Reporting : HTTP API\norganization reports

Events --> Identity : validate identity/scope
Registration --> Identity : validate identity/scope
Attendance --> Identity : validate identity/scope
Reporting --> Identity : validate identity/scope

Events --> EventData : own event/activity data
Registration --> RegistrationData : own registration/outbox data
Attendance --> AttendanceData : own attendance/certificate data
Reporting --> ReportingData : own projection data

Registration --> Events : published activity API\nfrozen admission snapshot API
Registration --> RabbitMQ : publish from outbox
RabbitMQ --> Billing : payment/refund request
Billing --> RabbitMQ : configured result
RabbitMQ --> Registration : payment/refund result
RabbitMQ --> Notification : delivery events
RabbitMQ --> Attendance : registration/activity facts
Attendance --> RabbitMQ : attendance/certificate facts
RabbitMQ --> Reporting : registration/payment/attendance facts

note bottom of PostgreSQL
One local cluster may host these isolated logical databases/schemas.
No service may read another service's tables or credentials.
end note

note bottom of RabbitMQ
Exchanges, routing keys, schemas and quarantine topology are defined in
the AsyncAPI contract and ADR-004. Retry delays are validated configuration.
end note

note bottom of DemoWeb
Optional presentation-only adapter. Uses server-side synthetic persona fixtures;
owns no domain state and has no database or broker access.
end note

legend right
|= Stereotype |= Prototype status |
| <<executable>> | Implemented domain service |
| <<mock>> | Contract-backed integration fake; not a domain service |
| <<presentation>> | Optional browser adapter; not a domain service |
endlegend
@enduml
